content.text:
## ✅ Corrected to the pseudo-element approach

You were right: flipping the whole `.is-home` container would also mirror the content.

I changed it to use a dedicated pseudo-element so only the decorative background art is flipped in RTL:

```css
.is-home::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  background-image: var(--vp-home-bg-image);
  ...
}

html[dir="rtl"] .is-home::before {
  background-position: left bottom;
  transform: scaleX(-1);
}
```

That keeps the homepage text and layout intact while mirroring the background image only.
